  "id": "kalindula",
  "name": "Kalindula (Zambian popular band music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Zambian popular band music that grew in the 1970s and 1980s from the string-band dance music of Luapula and Northern Province, named after the kalindula, a homemade bass instrument of those bands. Sung mainly in Bemba, it became the leading Zambian band sound on radio and record through groups and singers such as Amayenge, PK Chishala and Mashombe Blue Jeans; the electric bass card stands in for the kalindula bass in band line-ups.",
  "recipe": "classic Southern African mid-1970s kalindula, functional Song, African pop branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. single coil electric guitar, electric bass, machine hammered symmetric pattern organized rows full lathed both sides lathed drum kit. live tracking. dynamic moving-coil, tube pre, BBC broadcast console, vari-mu, passive program EQ. vinyl master cut.",
